                                        <p>
                                            Textbooks don't stand a chance against a classroom of kids raised on
                                            touchscreens. Our client, an edtech provider, watched this play out
                                            firsthand as lessons that should have sparked curiosity were instead met
                                            with glazed eyes and half-finished worksheets. So over 16 weeks, we built
                                            them an AR learning game that turns any classroom or living room into a lab.
                                            Point a tablet at an open desk, and a beating virtual heart appears to be
                                            dissected, or the solar system unfolds in orbit around a student's chair, or
                                            fractions become physical shapes they can rotate and stack with their
                                            fingers. For teachers, a live dashboard shows who's engaged, stuck, and
                                            where the curriculum needs to flex.
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                    <hr class="my-4" />
                                    <div>
                                        <h4 class="mb-3">Features</h4>
                                        <ul class="features-list">
                                            <li>Camera-based AR object overlay</li>
                                            <li>Curriculum-aligned lesson modules</li>
                                            <li>Interactive 3D learning models</li>
                                            <li>Real-time quizzes &amp; assessments</li>
                                            <li>Teacher dashboard &amp; progress tracking</li>
                                            <li>Adaptive difficulty engine</li>
                                            <li>Gamified badges &amp; reward streaks</li>
                                            <li>Multi-subject content library (STEM)</li>
                                            <li>Offline mode for classroom use</li>
                                            <li>Parental progress reports</li>
                                            <li>Multi-device compatibility (tablet/phone)</li>
                                            <li>COPPA-compliant data handling</li>
                                        </ul>
                                    </div>
                                    <hr class="my-4" />
                                    <div class="Glow-effect-5">
                                        <h4 class="mb-3">Technology Stack</h4>
                                        <ul class="features-list-2">
                                            <li>Unity 3D (AR Foundation)</li>
                                            <li>ARKit / ARCore</li>
                                            <li>C (Core Logic)</li>
                                            <li>Vuforia (Marker Tracking)</li>
                                            <li>Firebase (Auth &amp; Analytics)</li>
                                            <li>Node.js (Backend Services)</li>
                                            <li>PostgreSQL</li>
                                            <li>React (Teacher Dashboard)</li>
                                            <li>Blender (3D Model Creation)</li>
                                            <li>REST API Integration</li>
                                            <li>AWS S3 (Content Delivery)</li>
                                            <li>Figma (UI/UX Prototyping)</li>
